---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { settings } from '../lib/site.js';
---
<Base title="Privacy" description="What the Conceptual Studio website collects, why, and how to object.">
  <section class="page-head wrap grid"><h1>Privacy</h1><p class="lead">This site collects as little as possible.</p></section>
  <section class="wrap grid text-page">
    <div class="prose">
      <h2>Who is responsible</h2>
      <p>{settings.company.name}, London. Contact: <a class="link" href={`mailto:${settings.email}`}>{settings.email}</a>.</p>
      <h2>The enquiry form</h2>
      <p>When you send the form, I receive what you typed: your name, work email, organisation and project details. I use it only to reply and to prepare a quote, and I keep it as long as we’re talking or working together, plus whatever the law requires for business records.</p>
      <p>Form messages are delivered by Web3Forms, which acts as a processor and passes the message to my inbox. If you’d rather not use it, email me directly.</p>
      <h2>Cookies and analytics</h2>
      <p>The site sets no cookies of its own and doesn’t track you across other websites. If analytics are switched on, they use Cloudflare Web Analytics, which counts visits without cookies or personal profiles. You can object at any time by emailing me, or block it with any content blocker.</p>
      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>You can ask to see, correct or delete what I hold about you. Email me and I’ll reply within a month. You can also complain to the Information Commissioner’s Office.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
